practice.a:
Use the quotient rule: $\displaystyle\left(\frac{u}{v}\right)'=\frac{u'v-u v'}{v^{2}}$.
\[
u=5x^2-4,\; u'=10x;\qquad v=x,\; v'=1.
\]
\[
\frac{d}{dx}\left(\frac{5x^2-4}{x}\right)=\frac{(10x)(x)-(5x^2-4)(1)}{x^{2}}
=\frac{10x^{2}-5x^{2}+4}{x^{2}}
=\frac{5x^{2}+4}{x^{2}}
=5+\frac{4}{x^{2}}.
\]
